- The declared test command (`campaign/.venv/bin/python -m pytest`) can't run here: that venv has no pytest/astropy, and the 2018-era astropy source can't import under Python 3.12/numpy 2.5 (`collections.Mapping`, `np.product`, `distutils` removed). I verified via the pre-existing `C:/Windows/Temp/t7336` harness pattern (conftest swaps the repo's `decorators.py` into the system-installed astropy; `C:/Python312/python.exe3`, pytest 7.4.4), with its stale repo path repointed to this checkout. The harness lives outside the repo tree.
